"rempel@gmail.com" <rempel@gmail.com> wrote:
>Hey all - I am a devotee of the original nethack. One main reason is
>that in Nethack 2.2 and later, you can only cast a spell a certain
>number of times before it wears out. Is there anything you can do to
>"refresh" a spell? What's the point of a spellbook if you can't keep
>the spell and the spellbook disappears after you read it?

In Nethack 3.4.x, spells last 20k turns from the turn on which you
completed reading the spellbook and spellbooks can usually be read
multiple times before they become too faint to read; rereading a
spellbook resets your memory of the spell to last 20k turns beyond
the turn on which you completed rereading it.
